From cd806dc446d63d6ff040e89113af4cfac1a93a4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flavio Amurrio <25621374+FlavioAmurrioCS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 15:12:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Repair --pull for private registries and Docker Engine
 29+
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The --pull flag had three independent defects that combined to make it
unusable against anything but a public Docker Hub image on an older
daemon. All three are in the pull block of cmd/.../app/cmd/test.go.

1. The API version was pinned to 1.32.

go-dockerclient tags request fields with the minimum API version that
introduced them, and PullImageOptions.Platform carries `ver:"1.32"`.
Since --platform defaults to linux/$GOARCH it is never empty, so
pathVersionCheck wrote the request path as POST /v1.32/images/create
whenever the client had no API version of its own. Docker Engine 29
raised the minimum supported API version to 1.40 and rejects that with
"client version 1.32 is too old".

The client now asks the daemon which version it speaks and pins to that.
Probing is safe because /version is itself requested unversioned, so any
daemon answers it. DOCKER_API_VERSION still wins when set, and both a
failed probe and an unparseable version degrade to the previous
unversioned behavior rather than erroring.

Note that upgrading go-dockerclient does not fix this: v1.13.2 still
carries the same struct tag and an identical pathVersionCheck, and it
requires go 1.25 against this module's go 1.22.

2. Registry credentials were never sent.

The call passed a zero-value docker.AuthConfiguration{}, and
headersWithAuth skips any auth that is empty, so no X-Registry-Auth
header was sent and every pull was anonymous. Being logged in did not
help: the daemon performs the pull and never reads ~/.docker/config.json
— the client has to resolve credentials and forward them.

Credentials now come from the credential helper named by credHelpers or
credsStore, falling back to the plaintext auths entries in the Docker
config. Resolution failure is deliberately non-fatal so public images
keep pulling anonymously.

Fixes #253.

3. The registry host was dropped, sending every pull to Docker Hub.

Repository was set from ref.Context().RepositoryStr(), which strips the
host, and the Registry field is only serialized as a query parameter the
Engine API ignores — the daemon reads the host from fromImage. So
`--pull --image ghcr.io/org/app:tag` actually asked Docker Hub for
org/app, which surfaced as a confusing "pull access denied ... may
require 'docker login'" naming a repository the user never referenced.
Using ref.Context().Name() keeps the host in fromImage.

This is also the underlying cause of #193.

Verified with no DOCKER_API_VERSION set, against Engine 29.6.2
(API 1.55, minimum 1.40): a private ghcr.io image pulls and its tests
run; a Docker Hub short name still pulls, cold, with layer downloads; an
emptied DOCKER_CONFIG yields 401 against the correct ghcr.io host for
the private image while a public image still pulls anonymously; and
DOCKER_API_VERSION set to both 1.44 and 1.24 is honored verbatim.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cmd/container-structure-test/app/cmd/test.go | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cmd/container-structure-test/app/cmd/test.go b/cmd/container-structure-test/app/cmd/test.go
index 069b146..682bb7d 100644
--- a/cmd/container-structure-test/app/cmd/test.go
+++ b/cmd/container-structure-test/app/cmd/test.go
@@ -180,13 +180,29 @@ func run(out io.Writer) error {
 		if err != nil {
 			logrus.Fatalf("error connecting to daemon: %v", err)
 		}
+		if os.Getenv("DOCKER_API_VERSION") == "" {
+			if env, verErr := client.Version(); verErr == nil {
+				if versioned, vErr := docker.NewVersionedClientFromEnv(env.Get("ApiVersion")); vErr == nil {
+					client = versioned
+				}
+			}
+		}
+		registry := ref.Context().RegistryStr()
+		auth := docker.AuthConfiguration{}
+		if creds, credErr := docker.NewAuthConfigurationsFromCredsHelpers(registry); credErr == nil && creds != nil {
+			auth = *creds
+		} else if cfgs, cfgErr := docker.NewAuthConfigurationsFromDockerCfg(); cfgErr == nil {
+			if creds, ok := cfgs.Configs[registry]; ok {
+				auth = creds
+			}
+		}
 		if err = client.PullImage(docker.PullImageOptions{
 			Platform:     opts.Platform,
-			Repository:   ref.Context().RepositoryStr(),
+			Repository:   ref.Context().Name(),
 			Tag:          ref.Identifier(),
 			Registry:     ref.Context().RegistryStr(),
 			OutputStream: out,
-		}, docker.AuthConfiguration{}); err != nil {
+		}, auth); err != nil {
 			logrus.Fatalf("error pulling remote image %s: %s", opts.ImagePath, err.Error())
 		}
 	}
-- 
